WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
So Mossville was just [snaps] up there!

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.280
You name it, we had it.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.860
We had a great school, we had a great community, we had good public relations,

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.800
we had a good . . . We was getting a good education.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:22.040
And the education was . . . It wasn't second-class, but we got hand-me-down books.

6
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.440
But we learned.

7
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.240
You learned.

8
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.040
I mean you learned, because the teachers were so instrumental on us learning.

9
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.160
When it first started out in Mossville we only had three teachers.

10
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:41.880
One was Ms. Washington, one was Ms. [Billups?], and one was Ms. Mitchell.

11
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.540
And you learned what you had to learn.

12
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:55.040
I don't care if you didn't have good books, you wasn't going to be a dummy because that was important to them.

13
00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.000
And all they had to was tell your parents you weren't acting right, or you didn't act like you wanted to learn.

14
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.080
Next day you went to school, you were no problem.

15
00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:15.320
Because I think education back then was so important because they didn't have a lot of education.

16
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:21.880
Because my mom . . . I think my dad went to third grade, and he could write his name.

17
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:22.620
He could read.

18
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.320
He could write.

19
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.260
He could drive.

20
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.800
He could do it all.

21
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.020
And my mom . . . I don't know what grade she stopped in,

22
00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:39.240
but they were so rural and in Texas that they worked in the fields all the time.

23
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:48.540
So they didn't have too much education because it was ten girls and no boys and so they were . . . They worked hard in the fields.
